<h2>Fresh bulb or dried product: a sourcing checklist in one table</h2>
<p>The two forms are not fully interchangeable. If you sell onion as produce or need raw texture, fresh is the only option. If onion is an ingredient in soups, seasonings, snack coatings or ready meals, dried onion's shelf life and policy record make it worth trialling even where fresh is the habit. Many larger users run both.</p>
